DATA;
/* Synthetic model for the WAVE-PAGED aggregate prefetch (conway#561 §5).

   One IfcElementAssembly aggregating 12 IfcBuildingElementParts, each with
   its OWN representation, placement and profile — nothing shared — so every
   related product has a distinct `#ref` closure and "how much of the
   relationship has been paged" is observable by counting records.

   RelatedObjects also holds two IfcGroups: #150 in the middle of the list,
   #151 at the end of it. A group is an IfcObjectDefinition and not an
   IfcProduct, so the aggregates pass walks past it without extracting or
   yielding — see extractRelAggregateGeometryIncremental's
   `instanceof IfcProduct` guard.

   #150 is what makes "the n-th yield" and "the n-th related object"
   different indices, which is what a prefetch paged per stepper step has
   to get right. #151 is past the last yield entirely, so no later step
   exists for a wave to be carried by.

   Both groups are declared in the MIDDLE of the part records, deliberately:
   a test behind a narrow window can only tell "paged" from "not paged" for
   a record whose bytes nothing else pins, and the relationship's own record
   (last) and the assembly's (first) pin the two ends of the file for the
   relationship's whole life. */
#1=IFCPROJECT('CxLS067y1lcJywHUOaW903',$,'AggregatePagedPrefetch',$,$,$,$,(#20),#10);
#10=IFCUNITASSIGNMENT((#11));
#11=IFCSIUNIT(*,.LENGTHUNIT.,$,.METRE.);
#20=IFCGEOMETRICREPRESENTATIONCONTEXT($,'Model',3,1.0E-05,#21,$);
#21=IFCAXIS2PLACEMENT3D(#22,$,$);
#22=IFCCARTESIANPOINT((0.,0.,0.));
#23=IFCDIRECTION((0.,0.,1.));
/* Assembly: the relating object of the aggregate. */
#100=IFCELEMENTASSEMBLY('i4Ks9AHIF2WYzorh2Wuy52',$,'Assembly',$,$,#101,$,$,$,.NOTDEFINED.);
#101=IFCLOCALPLACEMENT($,#21);
/* Part 0: 1m box at x=0. */
